          <div><dt>GitHub</dt><dd><a href="https://github.com/amkashyap1220">github.com/amkashyap1220</a></dd></div>
        </dl>
        <a class="cta" href="/resume.pdf">Download resume <span class="mono">PDF</span></a>
      </section>

      <aside class="teaser" aria-labelledby="teaser-h">
        <p id="teaser-h" class="h-label">From my camera roll</p>
        <figure>
          <img src="/img/photos/fountain-480.webp" srcset="/img/photos/fountain-480.webp 480w, /img/photos/fountain-960.webp 960w" sizes="400px" width="1600" height="1480" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Buckingham Fountain spraying water on a sunny day, with the Chicago skyline behind it">
          <figcaption><span class="mono">Buckingham Fountain, Chicago</span> A few more are in <a href="#otc">Off the clock</a><span class="down" aria-hidden="true"> &darr;</span></figcaption>
        </figure>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <section class="featured" id="work" aria-labelledby="work-h">
      <h2 id="work-h" class="vh">Featured work</h2>

      <article class="h-lead" aria-labelledby="tm-h">
        <p class="kicker"><span class="k">My project</span> <span>PayPal AI Hackathon</span> <span>Nov 2026</span> <span>In progress</span></p>
        <h3 id="tm-h" class="hed-lead"><span class="proj">Open Tradesman<span class="vh">:</span></span> <span class="t"><span>Talk through the job in your language.</span> <span>The&nbsp;customer gets a priced estimate in theirs.</span></span></h3>
        <p class="dek">I&rsquo;m building a voice-first estimating app for tradespeople. Claude turns a spoken job description into an itemized, priced estimate, and PayPal invoicing handles the money, from the deposit and change orders to the final invoice.</p>
        <div class="h-body">
          <p>The AI does the tedious part: turning a rambling description into clean line items in someone else&rsquo;s language. I kept it out of the parts that need trust.</p>
        </div>

        <figure class="flow">
          <figcaption id="fig1" class="flow-cap"><span class="mono">Fig. 1</span> How a job moves through Open Tradesman, with each guardrail under the step it protects. Illustrative example.</figcaption>
          <ol class="steps">
            <li class="step">
              <p class="step-n mono"><b>01</b> Speak</p>
              <p class="said" lang="es">&ldquo;Cambio el calentador de agua de 40&nbsp;galones y me llevo el viejo.&rdquo;</p>
              <p class="h-note">The tradesperson describes the job out loud, in their own language.</p>
              <p class="guard"><span class="g">Guardrail</span> No invented measurements.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="step">
              <p class="step-n mono"><b>02</b> Match</p>
              <dl class="items">
                <div><dt>WH-40</dt><dd>Water heater, 40&nbsp;gal</dd></div>
                <div><dt>HAUL</dt><dd>Haul-away, old unit</dd></div>
              </dl>
              <p class="h-note">Claude picks each line item by id from the tradesperson&rsquo;s price book.</p>
              <p class="guard"><span class="g">Guardrail</span> Prices come only from the price book. Any SQL the AI writes runs read-only.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="step">
              <p class="step-n mono"><b>03</b> Estimate</p>
              <div class="est">
                <p class="est-h mono">Customer&rsquo;s copy, in English</p>
                <dl class="items items-est">
                  <div><dt>WH-40</dt><dd>Replace 40-gal water heater</dd><dd class="price">Book rate</dd></div>
                  <div><dt>HAUL</dt><dd>Haul away old unit</dd><dd class="price">Book rate</dd></div>
                </dl>
              </div>
              <p class="h-note">The same ids, each line priced from the price book and written in the customer&rsquo;s language.</p>
              <p class="guard"><span class="g">Guardrail</span> Anything that doesn&rsquo;t match the price book blocks the estimate from sending.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="step">
              <p class="step-n mono"><b>04</b> Get paid</p>
              <ol class="pay"><li>Deposit</li><li>Change order</li><li>Final invoice</li></ol>
              <p class="h-note">Each one goes out through the PayPal Invoicing API.</p>
              <p class="guard"><span class="g">Guardrail</span> PayPal webhooks are verified before they change anything.</p>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </figure>

        <p class="stack"><span>React PWA</span> <span>FastAPI</span> <span>Claude API</span> <span>PayPal Invoicing API</span> <span>Postgres</span></p>
        <a class="h-more" href="https://github.com/amkashyap1220/Open-Tradesman">Read the code on GitHub</a>
